module tasks.`2026-11-22-harness-space-paths`

task HarnessSpacePaths {
  title "Harness fixtures and Makefile break in checkouts whose path contains a space"
  verify $ cargo nextest run -p bboxy450-harness -E 'test(dream_proof_tools) | test(eof_cancels_a_pending_profile_factory)'
  paths "crates/bboxy450-harness", "Cargo.lock"
  brief """
    Our stand: subtract before you add; report what you removed. ROLE: EXECUTOR.

    ## Gap (Oracle, observed 2026-11-22)
    Every managed checkout lives under `~/Library/Application Support/bboxy450-term/run/implementation-workspaces/checkouts/<id>`, a path with a space. Harness tooling breaks there:
    - `bboxy450-harness::dream_proof_tools private_builder_source_and_publication_controls`: `scripts/dream-proof-tools.py:3618` raises "synthetic dependency fixture uses unescaped private paths" (also `test_q2_shim_resealed_inner_cross_bindings_still_refuse`, line 4249).
    - `bboxy450-harness::acp_face eof_cancels_a_pending_profile_factory_without_waiting_for_its_key_command` fails in the same checkout (evidence: svg-chrome checkout 01M82JAA2SY4ZYPE46E90NRZ7W, `target/svg-chrome-evidence/test-parity-amended.log`).
    - `make -C crates/bboxy450-harness land TARGET_DIR=<checkout>/target` split the space-bearing absolute path (chart-runtime report, reports/2026-11-22-chart-runtime.den).
    The same tests pass in a checkout under `~/mydev`.

    ## Do
    Make the harness fixtures and Makefile correct for paths containing spaces (quote/escape, never rely on the path being space-free). Add a regression that runs the affected fixtures from a temporary directory whose name contains a space. Land in harness, then bump term's pin with `make bump-harness`.

    ## Land
    Long commands detached. Harness `make land`, then term `make land`. Report at reports/2026-11-22-harness-space-paths.den, then `task_report`.


    ## Report from seat:01M83BEDTV3EGAJH0EDR0HEYXX

    [[Implement]] [[Done]] Harness fixtures and Make targets now work in paths containing spaces. The brief's nextest command passed 23 tests, the feature-enabled Dream and ACP regressions both passed, and the Make witness preserved the exact relative and absolute target path. Removed Make's word-splitting conversion, the fixture's space-free guard, unquoted ACP paths and persistent Dream fixture storage. Harness 3401be5f1386eb0aa34528b79cc01adb3cb6e252 and term fdf638b5d974e7f8957ca0150cfbc47296147f3d landed with verified signatures and clean worktrees. The landed term gate passed 1,994 nextest tests, and its refreshed receipt verified 999 native/Java TLC models. The full report is available in the machine-local KB. knowledge_commit returned exit 1 because reports/ is Git-ignored.

    ```json
